{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "30", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "38", "S": "58"}}, "news": [{"title": "Bengaluru's BDA apartments yet to fully turn EV infrastructure switch on", "para": "In Bengaluru, the trend of electric vehicle ownership is gaining momentum in apartment communities. A recent survey indicates that merely one in fifteen BDA complexes boasts a communal charging unit. The majority of residents rely on public charging stations or set up home solutions remotely. Notably, there's a strong enthusiasm among potential buyers for EVs in the coming years.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/bengalurus-bda-apartments-yet-to-fully-turn-ev-infrastructure-switch-on/134579407?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-74574/134579407.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Set up dedicated sub-registrar office at PMC headquarters: Builders\u2019 association urges Pune civic body", "para": "The Marathi Bandhkam Vyavsayik Association has formally approached the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) to establish a dedicated property registration office. According to Nitin Deshpande, the association's president, this development promises to streamline the property registration process, benefiting both builders and citizens. PMC is currently reviewing this proposal and will determine its viability while also coordinating with the Registration and Stamps Department for further insights.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/set-up-dedicated-sub-registrar-office-at-pmc-headquarters-builders-association-urges-pune-civic-body/134579351?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-194948/134579351.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Ease plan approvals for 70 metres buildings, says CREDAI-Ahmedabad", "para": "CREDAI Ahmedabad has urged the state government to streamline the approval process for highrise projects. The association highlighted delays in project timelines due to issues with Transferable Development Rights availability. They proposed a staged approval system separating plan scrutiny from TDR loading requirements. Developers requested that punitive actions not target builders for unrelated traffic issues caused by parking violations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/ease-plan-approvals-for-70-metres-buildings-says-credai-ahmedabad/134579181?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-112018/134579181.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}